Mark my words. You will never see another Bitcoin all-time high in your lifetime. The reported $6.3 billion Binance hack marked the end of an era. $BTC is now below $70,000. You may not trust fiat, but at least you don’t risk losing your entire savings overnight to a hack. Bitcoin has no meaningful use cases, and keeping it safe means storing it in your own wallet, the digital equivalent of cash under your mattress. Meanwhile, SpaceX, AI and other technologies offer far more exciting opportunities for capital. Bitcoin had its run. I’m not saying it goes to zero, not even close. I’m saying it will never make a new high.

@Ek321979 A 20-year pattern is far from reliable, especially when it comes to technology. New technologies have emerged, while Bitcoin has failed to evolve into a real payment system. What doesn’t evolve, devolves.

Be honest with yourself. If you had to choose between buying SpaceX or Bitcoin today and holding for the next 10 years, which would you trust more? Four years ago, we didn’t have these kinds of alternatives. Now we do. Capital is limited, and Bitcoin is no longer competing with the same investment opportunities it was competing with four years ago.

